jobs_results.description:
Are we the best-kept secret in Malaga? We sure like to think so.

We are one of the world’s largest globally diversified natural resources companies and a major producer and marketer of more than 60 commodities across several countries. Our latest addition is a new office in beautiful Malaga, and we currently have multiple openings for driven and passionate IT professionals like you.

Our motto is Advancing careers. Advancing everyday life. Whether you are at the start of your career or already experienced, we want to hear from you.

We are serious about finding the right people and confident that we have a lot to offer. After all, we are an employer of choice. (more details below 😊)

The role in a nutshell

In this role, you will be instrumental in designing, implementing, and managing SAP development solutions for Glencores diverse systems.

Your expertise in SAP development technologies across different SAP modules will be crucial in driving successful new development initiatives... and maintaining the current SAP landscape.

More specifically, you will be expected to:
• Create new SAP solutions to meet customer needs and requirements;
• Enhance existing custom SAP solutions in response to customer requests;
• Utilise your expertise to efficiently resolve incidents with custom SAP solutions;
• Contribute to the ongoing improvement of business processes and the SAP solution;
• Delivery of end-to-end solutions with minimal supervision;
• Participate in continuous improvement initiatives and other ad hoc related-projects.

Do you have what it takes?
• Completed studies in a relevant field;
• A minimum of 3 years of experience in SAP ECC or SAP S4 Hana;
• Demonstrated experience developing solutions in at least one of the process areas such as FI/CO, PS, MM, PM or SD;
• Exposure to a variety of ABAP development technologies – ALV reports, Interfacing (IDOC and API), Conversions, Adobe Forms/Smart Forms, custom enhancements, and modifications;
• An experience with SAPUI5/Fiori development will be highly regarded;
• Ability to work independently under limited supervision to deliver high quality SAP solutions to meet customer needs, in line with defined architectural standards;
• Ability to collaborate effectively and work as part of a global team;
• Strong attention to detail and a positive attitude;
• Critical thinking and analytical problem-solving skills.

Language : As you will be part of a global team, you must be able to communicate fluently in English (verbal and written). Knowledge of other languages such as French, German and/or Spanish is desirable.

Travel: Some occasional travelling may be required.

Wondering what’s in it for you?
• Hybrid Work
• Very competitive compensation and annual salary review
• Health Insurance coverage for you and your dependents (employee + spouse/partner and children)
• Life Insurance
• Growth opportunities (career progression, tuition assistance, language courses, training and certifications, etc.)
• Relocation assistance

We are building a multi-cultural and multi-disciplinary dream team in which you will have the opportunity to collaborate with domain experts - enjoying all the perks of a big company with the energy of a start-up. And yes, that includes state-of-the-art equipment, access to a fitness program, reimbursement of public transportation for commuting to work and all the coffee you can drink (but if you prefer tea, we’ll sort something out for you) 😊

Get to know us

Recently, Glencore’s Zinc division has embarked in a system replacement globally with the implementation of SAP S/4 HANA and Coupa as the main backbone to support industrial business operations globally. The solution has been deployed in some parts of the business in Q4 2023 and we are continuing our journey to roll-out the global solution to all sites to cover Australia, Spain, UK, Germany, Italy and Canada.

The global AMS team is formed by functional teams located in the north of Spain, Australia and Canada, combined with a central team located in Malaga. This new Group supports the business users globally from an applications management support perspective.

Glencore encourages diversity and provides an inclusive workplace. Accommodations are available upon request for applicants with special needs. recruitment@glencore.ca

Interviews may start prior to the closing date

